  "description": "SIYFOY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C152 H168 Dy4 N12 O22,5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.549-3.892 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.26-111.88°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C152H168Dy4N12O22·5(C2H3N).",
